R"VG(
# letter_events_private.vg (H-04, the second pass): the letter's register for a family's everyday (the history's private kinds besides the
# births, weddings, moves and deaths): an illness got over, a hurt, a child apprenticed, a house built or burnt or mended, a quarrel
# with the neighbours, a journey and back, a betrothal. The warmest news a letter carries; low in salience, so they come in the
# quiet years. `$e.a` the one it was about (never the reader), `$e.b` the other where there is one, `$e.what` the kind's own word.

# ---- an illness, got over -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.illness
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} had {let.ill.of} {deathwhen}, and is over it. {let.ill.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} was laid up with {let.ill.of} for [a week|nine days|half a moon], and is up again and cross about it. {let.ill.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) We were worried about {$e.a} {deathwhen}: {let.ill.of}, and a bad one. {let.ill.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person=1) I was ill {deathwhen}, {let.ill.of}, and I am better, and that is all I will say about it.
let.ill.of
  ($e.what=fever) a fever
  ($e.what=cough) a cough that would not shift
  ($e.what=spots) the spots
  ($e.what=flux) the flux
  ($e.what=chill) a chill
  ($e.what=earache) an earache
  ($e.what=toothache) a toothache
  ($e.what=rash) a rash
  ($e.what=headaches) the headaches
  ($e.what!=fever $e.what!=cough $e.what!=spots $e.what!=flux $e.what!=chill $e.what!=earache $e.what!=toothache $e.what!=rash $e.what!=headaches) what the healer calls {$e.what}
let.ill.coda (share=0.8)
  The healer gave {$e.a:obj} {crop2} steeped in {drink}, which tastes of the floor and works.
  We kept {$e.a:obj} warm and fed and quiet, which was the hard part.
  {god} be thanked, and the healer, a little.
  {$e.a:name} is thinner and in a temper, so {$e.a:name} is well again.
  We hung {colour.holy} thread over the bed, as the old ones say to.
  It went through the house after, so we have all had a turn, and the {beast} too.
  (age>=industrial) The doctor came twice and charged three times, in {coin}.

# ---- a hurt -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.injury
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} {let.inj.how} {deathwhen}. {let.inj.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} {let.inj.how}, {let.inj.doing}. {let.inj.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person=1) I {let.inj.how}, {let.inj.doing}. It is mending, and so is my temper.
let.inj.how
  ($e.what=arm) broke an arm
  ($e.what=leg) broke a leg
  ($e.what=hand) cut a hand to the bone
  ($e.what=back) did something to the back that will not undo
  ($e.what=eye) hurt an eye
  ($e.what=head) cracked a head on a beam
  ($e.what=foot) crushed a foot
  ($e.what=ribs) broke two ribs
  ($e.what=shoulder) put a shoulder out
  ($e.what=wrist) twisted a wrist
let.inj.doing (share=0.8)
  falling off the roof, mending what the wind took
  under the cart, being helpful
  with {tool}, which has been put away
  chasing the {beast}, which got away
  at the {craft}, which was nobody's fault but everybody says whose
  (cold=1) on the ice by {$e.a.home}
  bringing the {herd} down off the hill in the dark
  in a fight about nothing at {festival}
let.inj.coda (share=0.8)
  The bone-setter came and set it, and swore by {god}, and set it again.
  It is mending, slowly, and {$e.a:name} is not.
  {$e.a:name} will carry the scar and the story both.
  We have done all the work since, the {herd} included, and heard about the pain all day.
  (age>=industrial) The doctor says six weeks; {$e.a:name} says six days.

# ---- a child apprenticed ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.apprentice
  (tense=past) {$e.a} has gone as apprentice to a {$e.what}. {let.app.coda}
  (tense=past) We have bound {$e.a} to a {$e.what} for {n} years. {let.app.coda}
  (tense=past) {$e.a} is to be a {$e.what}, it is settled. {let.app.coda}
let.app.coda (share=0.8)
  The master is strict and fair, they say, and has a wife who feeds them on {food}.
  {$e.a:name} cried the first night and boasted the second.
  It is a good trade, and better than {craft}, which is mine.
  {$e.a:name} sleeps over the shop and comes home on feast days with burnt fingers and new words.
  The fee was {n} {coin} and a {vessel.one.n} of {food}, and worth it, we hope.
  The old ones say it is too young; the old ones started younger, with the {herd}.

# ---- the house -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.house
  (tense=present $e.what=built) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} built a house at last, {let.house.which}. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=bought) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} bought the house {let.house.where}. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=sold) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} sold the old house, and cried, and spent the money. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=past $e.what=burnt) {$e.a:poss} house burned {deathwhen}; they got out with the {herd} and nothing else. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=past $e.what=flooded) The water got into {$e.a:poss} house {deathwhen}, to the height of the table. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=mended) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} mended the house from the ground up, and it looks like a new one with old manners. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=room) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} built a room on the back of the house, for the children or the {herd}, it is not decided. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=roof) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} a new roof, and {talk:$e.a} of nothing else. {let.house.coda}
  (tense=present $e.what=moved) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} moved house, three streets over, with the {vessel} carried by hand. {let.house.coda}
let.house.which (share=0.8)
  of {walls.of}, with {roofs}
  with {motif.over} over the door
  (has:$e.a.home.landmark) by {$e.a.home.landmark}
  on the edge of town where the {herd} can be heard
  small, and dry, and paid for
let.house.where
  by the market
  (has:$e.a.home.landmark) by {$e.a.home.landmark}
  at the top of the street
  (has:$e.a.home.quarter) in {$e.a.home.quarter}
  that the old {$me.trade} had
let.house.coda (share=0.8)
  ($e.what=built|$e.what=bought|$e.what=moved|$e.what=room|$e.what=roof|$e.what=mended) We all went to look and say the right things about the {roofs}.
  ($e.what=built|$e.what=bought|$e.what=moved) The neighbours brought {food}; it is the custom, and they wanted to see inside.
  ($e.what=built|$e.what=bought|$e.what=moved) We hung {colour.holy} cloth on the door, for luck in it.
  ($e.what=built|$e.what=bought|$e.what=room) It will be cold in the cold months and hot in the hot, like every {let.house.n}.
  ($e.what=burnt|$e.what=flooded) They are with us for now, and the {herd} are with the neighbours.
  ($e.what=burnt|$e.what=flooded) We sent {vessel} and {food} and the old {garment.n} nobody wears.
  ($e.what=sold) The new people have painted the door {colour.any}, which Mother would not have stood for.
  {proverb}, the old ones said, and the young ones did not listen.

let.house.n (people=1)
  (age<=medieval) house
  (age>=industrial) house
  (plan=round age<=medieval) round house
  (plan=square age<=medieval) long house
  (plan=court) courtyard house

# ---- a quarrel ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.quarrel
  (tense=past has:$e.b $e.a.person!=1 $e.b.person!=1) {$e.a} and {$e.b} are not speaking, over {let.q.of}. {let.q.coda}
  (tense=past has:$e.b $e.a.person!=1 $e.b.person!=1) {$e.a} has fallen out with {$e.b}, over {let.q.of}, and the whole street has taken sides. {let.q.coda}
  (tense=past !has:$e.b $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} has quarrelled with the neighbours over {let.q.of}. {let.q.coda}
  (tense=past has:$e.b $e.b.person=1) {$e.a} and I have fallen out, over {let.q.of}. {let.q.mine}
  (tense=past has:$e.b $e.a.person=1) I have fallen out with {$e.b}, over {let.q.of}. {let.q.mine}
  (tense=past !has:$e.b $e.a.person=1) I have quarrelled with the neighbours over {let.q.of}. {let.q.mine}
let.q.of
  ($e.what=wall) a wall
  ($e.what=water) the water
  ($e.what=debt) a debt
  ($e.what=inheritance) an inheritance
  ($e.what=dog) a dog
  ($e.what=boundary) a boundary stone
  ($e.what=marriage) a marriage
  ($e.what=tree) a tree that leans
  ($e.what=noise) the noise
  ($e.what=path) a path
  ($e.what=beasts) the {herd}
  ($e.what=loan) a loan of {vessel}
let.q.coda (share=0.8)
  I keep out of it with my {herd}, which offends both of them.
  It will go to {hall} if nobody laughs first.
  The {beast} is the only one who still visits both houses.
  They swore {oath}, both of them, and both meant it.
  It is the most interesting thing to happen {season.this}.
  Mother would have banged their heads together over a {vessel.one.n}.

let.q.mine (share=0.8)
  I was right, and I will go on being right until they admit it over {drink}.
  We will make it up at {festival}; we always do.
  Mother would have banged our heads together and given us {food} after.
  I have sworn {oath} not to speak first, and I am regretting the oath already.

# ---- a journey and back --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.journey
  (tense=present $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} been to {$e.place2} {let.j.why}, and is back. {let.j.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person!=1) {$e.a} went to {$e.place2} {let.j.why} and came home {deathwhen} with {let.j.with}. {let.j.coda}
  (tense=past $e.a.person=1) I have been to {$e.place2} {let.j.why}, and I am back, and my feet will never forgive me. {let.j.coda}
let.j.why
  ($e.what=trade) to trade
  ($e.what=kin) to see the family
  ($e.what=pilgrimage) on pilgrimage
  ($e.what=work) for the work
  ($e.what=fair) for the fair
  ($e.what=study) to study
  ($e.what=law) about a lawsuit
  ($e.what=wedding) for a wedding
  ($e.what=funeral) for a burying
  ($e.what=doctor) to see a healer
let.j.with (share=0.8)
  a {garment.n} nobody here would wear
  three new words and a cough
  {vessel.one} of {food} that did not survive the road
  stories enough for the winter
  nothing, having spent it all
  a great opinion of {$e.place2} and a low one of us
let.j.coda (share=0.8)
  The roads are worse than they were, everyone says, and the {beast} agrees.
  {$e.place2} is very grand and very dear, by the sound of it.
  They eat {food} there with everything, apparently.
  We heard all about it, twice, over the {food}.
  It was {n} days each way, and the {beast} went lame on the second.

# ---- a betrothal ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

letter.betrothal
  (tense=present has:$e.b $e.b.person!=1) {$e.a} {be:$e.a} promised to {$e.b:name}. {let.bet.coda}
  (tense=past has:$e.b $e.a.person!=1 $e.b.person!=1) It is settled: {$e.a} and {$e.b:name}, at {festival} next year. {let.bet.coda}
  (tense=present has:$e.b $e.b.person!=1) {$e.a} {have:$e.a} given {$e.a:poss} word to {$e.b:name}, a {$e.b.trade}. {let.bet.coda}
  (tense=present has:$e.b $e.b.person=1) I am promised to {$e.a:name}, a {$e.a.trade}, and I have not stopped smiling since. {let.bet.coda}
let.bet.coda (share=0.8)
  The families have shaken hands and are counting the cost in {herd}.
  We gave them {vessel.one} of {drink} and our blessing, in that order.
  {blessing}, we said, and they blushed.
  Nobody is surprised but the two of them and the {beast}.
  The old ones are already arguing about the feast, and whether {food} will do.
  We sent to {holyplace} for a lucky day, and they sent back three.
)VG"
